{"name":"Glasgow Fog","hex":"#bdb8ae","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"fog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A thick cloud that forms near the ground; the obscurity of such a cloud.","A mist or film clouding a surface."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To become covered with or as if with fog.","To become obscured in condensation or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/fog"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glasgow","blocks":[{"text":"Glasgow is the most populous city in Scotland, located on the banks of the River Clyde in west central Scotland. It is the third-most populous city in the United Kingdom and comprises 23 wards which represent the areas within the city boundaries. Glasgow is a leading city in Scotland for university education and research, finance, industry, commerce, shopping, culture and fashion, and was commonly referred to as the \"second city of the British Empire\" for much of the Victorian and Edwardian eras."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Glasgow_-_aerial_-_2025-04-17_14.jpg/330px-Glasgow_-_aerial_-_2025-04-17_14.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glasgow","wikidata":"Q4093"},{"title":"Fog","blocks":[{"text":"Fog is a visible aerosol consisting of tiny water droplets or ice crystals held in the air near the Earth's surface. Fog can be considered a type of low-lying cloud usually resembling stratus and is heavily influenced by nearby bodies of water, topography, and wind conditions. In turn, fog affects many human activities, such as shipping, travel, and warfare. Recent atmospheric research indicates that fog also functions as an active aquatic ecosystem. Fog droplets harbor microbiomes where bacteria actively grow, divide, and interact with atmospheric chemistry."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/51/A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg/330px-A_foggy_winter_morning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fog","wikidata":"Q37477"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Glasgow%40JamesWatt%2CPrinzAlbert%2CQueenVictoria%2CRobertPeel.jpg/500px-Glasgow%40JamesWatt%2CPrinzAlbert%2CQueenVictoria%2CRobertPeel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Glasgow%40JamesWatt%2CPrinzAlbert%2CQueenVictoria%2CRobertPeel.jpg/1280px-Glasgow%40JamesWatt%2CPrinzAlbert%2CQueenVictoria%2CRobertPeel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Glasgow%40JamesWatt%2CPrinzAlbert%2CQueenVictoria%2CRobertPeel.jpg/500px-Glasgow%40JamesWatt%2CPrinzAlbert%2CQueenVictoria%2CRobertPeel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlasgow%40JamesWatt%2CPrinzAlbert%2CQueenVictoria%2CRobertPeel.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Glasgow_City_Chambers_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4865333.jpg/330px-Glasgow_City_Chambers_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4865333.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Glasgow_City_Chambers_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4865333.jpg/330px-Glasgow_City_Chambers_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4865333.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGlasgow_City_Chambers_-_geograph.org.uk_-_4865333.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Glasgow_Science_Centre_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2617051.jpg/500px-Glasgow_Science_Centre_-_geograph.org.uk_-_2617051.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedi